        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(nostr): trim private test seams",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Nostr plugin retained unused profile validation/sanitization helpers, test-only rate-limit exports, redundant key helpers, and aggregate exports with no production callers. Their tests made those private seams look supported and kept 13 stale entries in the unused-export baseline.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis maintainer-requested dead-code sweep removes the unused production paths, keeps the profile event builder and HTTP context private, imports profile conversion helpers from their owning module, and resets the profile limiter through the existing test dependency mock. Shared limiter behavior remains covered by its owner tests.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. The Nostr plugin has a smaller private surface and less redundant test code while retaining profile publishing, importing, routing, validation, and rate limiting.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcaqh5n8v56zwtmqnrnb4jw`:\n  - 6 focused Nostr test files passed, 105 tests total\n  - targeted `pnpm check:changed` passed extension production/test typechecks, extension and script lint, package/API guards, database/storage guards, and runtime cycle checks\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` reports only unrelated current-main baseline drift in MCP app exports and a stale session-utils entry; no Nostr symbol remains.\n- Direct `nostr-tools 2.23.9` source/type inspection confirms `nip19.npubEncode` accepts a hex string and `decode(npub)` returns the original hex string.\n- Open PR overlap audit found only two Nostr outbound text-sanitization PRs; neither touches this patch's files or invariants.\n- Fresh dirty-tree `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview: clean, confidence `0.96`.\n- Fresh exact-commit `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview: clean, confidence `0.94`.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Changelog: not required for this internal cleanup.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. No transcript attached.\n",
